A||||6||sqoach||Question for anyone with power locks||||5||
Z||000000||sqoach||08-06-2001||04:18 PM||||How many of you actually use the passenger side p/l switch? I just used mine for the first time last night. I was getting something out of the passenger seat, and locked it up for the night. The letters on it are near perfect. On the driver's side, they're faded pretty bad. Is it just me or what?<P>Sorry if this is a dumb question, just curious.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-06-2001||04:22 PM||||I actually use mine rather often. I almost always unlock the passenger side first (using the key) to let my wife in, then hit the unlock button before closing the door. That way when I walk back to the driver's side, the door is open.<P>Also, my passenger side doesn't unlock completely when I press the switch on the drivers door (or the passenger's). Does anyone know if I just need to replace the solinoid or what?<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-06-2001||05:35 PM||||theres a lot on that. just do a search. most of the time a good cleanout and lube job inside the door fixes it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Capt Fiero||08-06-2001||06:07 PM||||Both of mine are faded pretty bad, because just like minngreengt I use to unlock the passanger side door first for all my dates and once they got in I would tap the unlock button to unlock the drivers door for myself.  Granted now I have an alarm that has keyless options so I just arm the car as I walk away and it locks the doors and disarm it as I walk up and it unlocks em, even has keyless trunk.  If anyone ever has a choice of getting keyless entry with an alarm, always get it, I don't know how I lived without it.  <p>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-06-2001||08:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B><P>Also, my passenger side doesn't unlock completely when I press the switch on the drivers door (or the passenger's). Does anyone know if I just need to replace the solinoid or what?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just remove the door panel and clean the linkage. You can also lube them with a dry graphite or very light grease. You don't want to use something that will hold dust/dirt or they will "slow down" again.<BR>Also works on the power windows too.  TIf you clean the tracks the windows will go up and down faster.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||08-07-2001||01:12 AM||||Oh, so that explains it. I haven't taken a girl out anywhere in my Fiero. In fact, haven't had a date since I've had it. Oh well...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kelvin Vivian||08-07-2001||01:29 AM||||I just replaced the driver-side "LOCK/UNLOCK" button today in the GT. I grabbed a couple of pretty good switches out of a wrecked 86 GT, I'll change the passenger-side switch tomorrow. <P>They are not too difficult to change. Takes less than five minutes once you know how.<P>KV<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd, burgundy/grey<BR>88 GT T-top, 5-spd, bright red/beechwood<P>||||reg||1
